{"@odata.context":"https://localhost:7066/api/$metadata#news(Category(),CreatedBy(),Tags())","@odata.count":6,"value":[{"NewsArticleId":"d425467c6e9c47d8b289","NewsTitle":"New Research Findings Shed Light on STEM 8888","Headline":"New Research Findings Shed Light on STEM","CreatedDate":"2026-02-25T21:33:24.873+07:00","NewsContent":"ai , chatgpt , gemini","NewsSource":"N/A","NewsImage":null,"Views":6,"ImageUrl":"https://localhost:7066/images/ea3ac561-136f-4b3b-b1de-5562222098fa.png","CategoryId":1,"NewsStatus":true,"CreatedById":6,"UpdatedById":null,"ModifiedDate":null,"Category":{"CategoryId":1,"CategoryName":"Academic newsa","CategoryDescription":"This category can include articles about research findings, faculty appointments and promotions, and other academic-related announcements.","ParentCategoryId":1,"IsActive":true},"CreatedBy":{"AccountId":6,"AccountName":"thang","AccountEmail":"thang@gmail.com","AccountRole":1,"AccountPassword":"111"},"Tags":[{"TagId":2,"TagName":"Technology","Note":"Technology Note"},{"TagId":4,"TagName":"Innovation","Note":"Innovation Note"}]},{"NewsArticleId":"08992edf22fe4f8586d8","NewsTitle":"New Research Findings Shed Light on STEM 8888","Headline":"New Research Findings Shed Light on STEM","CreatedDate":"2026-02-24T23:34:50.343+07:00","NewsContent":"ai , chatgpt , gemini","NewsSource":"N/A","NewsImage":null,"Views":4,"ImageUrl":"https://localhost:7066/images/ea3ac561-136f-4b3b-b1de-5562222098fa.png","CategoryId":1,"NewsStatus":true,"CreatedById":6,"UpdatedById":null,"ModifiedDate":null,"Category":{"CategoryId":1,"CategoryName":"Academic newsa","CategoryDescription":"This category can include articles about research findings, faculty appointments and promotions, and other academic-related announcements.","ParentCategoryId":1,"IsActive":true},"CreatedBy":{"AccountId":6,"AccountName":"thang","AccountEmail":"thang@gmail.com","AccountRole":1,"AccountPassword":"111"},"Tags":[{"TagId":2,"TagName":"Technology","Note":"Technology Note"},{"TagId":4,"TagName":"Innovation","Note":"Innovation Note"}]},{"NewsArticleId":"31b930d264344e098361","NewsTitle":"Alumni Association Launches Mentorship Program for Recent Graduates 456","Headline":"Alumni Association Launches Mentorship Program for Recent Graduates","CreatedDate":"2026-02-24T20:46:22.51+07:00","NewsContent":"The Alumni Association of University FU recently unveiled a new mentorship program aimed at providing support and guidance to recent graduates as they navigate the transition from academia to the professional world.\r\n\r\nThe program pairs recent graduates with experienced alumni mentors based on their career interests and goals, ensuring tailored guidance for each mentee.\r\n\r\nIn addition to one-on-one mentorship, the program offers workshops on resume building, interview preparation, and networking strategies to equip graduates with essential skills for success.\r\n\r\nThe mentorship program also facilitates networking events where mentees can expand their professional connections and learn from alumni who have excelled in their respective fields.\r\n\r\nBy fostering a supportive network of alumni mentors, the program aims to empower recent graduates to navigate the challenges of the job market, enhance their professional growth, and build lasting connections within their industries.\r\n\r\nThe launch of this mentorship program by the Alumni Association of University Y underscores the commitment to nurturing the success of its graduates beyond graduation, creating a strong community of support and guidance for the next generation of professionals.","NewsSource":"Internet","NewsImage":null,"Views":4,"ImageUrl":"https://localhost:7066/images/dab21b15-b057-4f56-a3e5-fd298beabc72.png","CategoryId":4,"NewsStatus":true,"CreatedById":6,"UpdatedById":null,"ModifiedDate":null,"Category":{"CategoryId":4,"CategoryName":"Alumni News","CategoryDescription":"This category can include articles about the achievements and accomplishments of former students and alumni, such as graduations, job promotions and career successes.","ParentCategoryId":4,"IsActive":true},"CreatedBy":{"AccountId":6,"AccountName":"thang","AccountEmail":"thang@gmail.com","AccountRole":1,"AccountPassword":"111"},"Tags":[{"TagId":5,"TagName":"Campus Life","Note":"Campus Life Note"},{"TagId":7,"TagName":"Alumni ","Note":"Alumni News"},{"TagId":8,"TagName":"Events","Note":"University Events"},{"TagId":9,"TagName":"Resources","Note":"Campus Resources"}]},{"NewsArticleId":"205a854057824eaf82ab","NewsTitle":"Alumni Association Launches Mentorship Program for Recent Graduates 123","Headline":"Alumni Association Launches Mentorship Program for Recent Graduates","CreatedDate":"2026-02-23T08:54:02.767+07:00","NewsContent":"The Alumni Association of University FU recently unveiled a new mentorship program aimed at providing support and guidance to recent graduates as they navigate the transition from academia to the professional world.\r\n\r\nThe program pairs recent graduates with experienced alumni mentors based on their career interests and goals, ensuring tailored guidance for each mentee.\r\n\r\nIn addition to one-on-one mentorship, the program offers workshops on resume building, interview preparation, and networking strategies to equip graduates with essential skills for success.\r\n\r\nThe mentorship program also facilitates networking events where mentees can expand their professional connections and learn from alumni who have excelled in their respective fields.\r\n\r\nBy fostering a supportive network of alumni mentors, the program aims to empower recent graduates to navigate the challenges of the job market, enhance their professional growth, and build lasting connections within their industries.\r\n\r\nThe launch of this mentorship program by the Alumni Association of University Y underscores the commitment to nurturing the success of its graduates beyond graduation, creating a strong community of support and guidance for the next generation of professionals.","NewsSource":"Internet","NewsImage":null,"Views":7,"ImageUrl":"https://localhost:7066/images/dab21b15-b057-4f56-a3e5-fd298beabc72.png","CategoryId":4,"NewsStatus":true,"CreatedById":6,"UpdatedById":null,"ModifiedDate":null,"Category":{"CategoryId":4,"CategoryName":"Alumni News","CategoryDescription":"This category can include articles about the achievements and accomplishments of former students and alumni, such as graduations, job promotions and career successes.","ParentCategoryId":4,"IsActive":true},"CreatedBy":{"AccountId":6,"AccountName":"thang","AccountEmail":"thang@gmail.com","AccountRole":1,"AccountPassword":"111"},"Tags":[{"TagId":5,"TagName":"Campus Life","Note":"Campus Life Note"},{"TagId":7,"TagName":"Alumni ","Note":"Alumni News"},{"TagId":8,"TagName":"Events","Note":"University Events"},{"TagId":9,"TagName":"Resources","Note":"Campus Resources"}]},{"NewsArticleId":"70fe3cf127cf4ff89c38","NewsTitle":"New Research Findings Shed Light on STEM","Headline":"New Research Findings Shed Light on STEM","CreatedDate":"2026-02-22T10:16:00.497+07:00","NewsContent":"Groundbreaking research conducted by the Research Department of FU has unveiled significant findings in the field of STEM, offering fresh insights that could revolutionize current understanding and practices.\r\n\r\nThe success of this research is attributed to the collaborative efforts of a multidisciplinary team, showcasing the institution's commitment to fostering cutting-edge research. The newly uncovered knowledge has the potential to influence Math, Engineering, Technology and shape future research endeavors, positioning the Research Department of FU as a leader in the advancement of STEM.\r\n\r\nThe research findings stand as a testament to the institution's dedication to impactful research and its contribution to the global knowledge base in STEM.","NewsSource":"a","NewsImage":null,"Views":11,"ImageUrl":"https://localhost:7066/images/af2d5568-7257-4e43-a9cb-d130a62d8b5f.png","Categ